      "message": "feat(setup): pick the work offset (G54-G59) a setup posts at\n\nA setup now stores its program offset (SetupDef.work_offset, default\nAuto = the inferred per-operation law, so every existing document and\ngolden posts byte-identically). The one slot law, wcs_slot(world, setup,\nparams), reads the pick first; wcs_context and every caller (generation,\nstamp, spindle law, machine travel check, the post, the #315 rotation\nclause) follow it.\n\n- SetSetupWorkOffset: undoable, validated at construction; a datum\n  transfer copies the source's pick.\n- Setups page: a Work offset combo per setup (Auto, G54..G59).\n- Project v51: \"work_offset\": \"G55\" on the setup payload, omitted when\n  unpicked; v50 steps up (absent = Auto); an unknown word is corrupt.\n- Refusals by name: a height measured from another slot than its\n  setup's pick (verification gate); two setups of one NC file posting\n  the same word from different placements (one-file/script post; per-op\n  files exempt).\n- Setup sheet: WCS OFFSETS names the program offset.\n\nFixes #196\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
